From 4eac9111da8a65ea086e1a9957b0400786609b7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Farhan <farhanabdm@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:35:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gi): add custom characters

Add a "Custom Character" option to the Add Character dialog. A custom
character reuses the talents, passives, constellations, conditionals and
formulas of an existing template character, with its own name, element,
weapon type, rarity, level 90 base HP/ATK/DEF and ascension stat.

- Definitions are stored in localStorage (go_customCharacters) and
  appended to the character key lists at load time.
- Stats are derived from the template's level curves and scaled to the
  given level 90 values.
- Sheets record the arguments passed to dataObjForCharacterSheet so a
  template's data can be rebuilt under the custom key.
- Images and texts fall back to the template; names are injected into
  i18n.
- Creating, editing or deleting a custom character reloads GO.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Asb8vZRqeTYT9zLpVizGNv
